englishSenses.definition:
n. An oversounding, or a misuse, of the letter r;
   specifically (Phylol.), the tendency, exhibited in the Indo-European
   languages, to change s to r, as wese to were.

v. t. To rub, grind, bruise, or thrash.
v. t. To rub or grind to a very fine or impalpable powder;
   to pulverize and comminute thoroughly.
